<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Yellowjacket Trail</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:134-3: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.301623" lon="-121.742635"><ele>1217.6</ele><name>Mazama Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:mazama-sno-park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 136; quote: Following a route cut through the forest from the Timberline road to the White River</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.301460" lon="-121.741130"><ele>1216.3</ele><name>Timberline road at Highway 26</name><desc>source: OSM node 37466014, Timberline Highway junction; confidence: high; pdf_page: 136; quote: starts near the Timberline road-Highway 26 junction</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.302320" lon="-121.738140"><ele>1230.3</ele><name>Trail leaves the Timberline road</name><desc>source: OSM node 37518682, where unnamed track 1305441119 leaves the Timberline Highway (USFS SNO-663 fragments lie along it); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 136; quote: The trail, starting up the Timberline road about 80 yards from Highway 26, enters dense forest.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.305560" lon="-121.732400"><ele>1248.0</ele><name>White Away Trail junction</name><desc>source: OSM Whiteaway Trail (way 244102652) north end; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 135; quote: This road climbs through forest to a junction with the West Yellowjacket Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.299410" lon="-121.725210"><ele>1302.5</ele><name>Above the West Clearcut</name><desc>source: USFS SNO-663 fragment (Yellowjacket Nordic); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 136; quote: It continues through the trees above the West Clearcut to the Snow Bunny Trail.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.301720" lon="-121.719610"><ele>1311.1</ele><name>Snow Bunny Trail crossing</name><desc>source: north end of the West Clearcut road (OSM way 5284185) on the Snow Bunny Trail (OSM Timberline East Leg), start of USFS SNO-663 piece; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 136; quote: continue uphill 0.4 mile to where signs mark the crossing of the Yellowjacket Trail. Immediately back, at a sharp reverse angle to the left, is a road that leads 0.4 mile to the West Clearcut</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.299190" lon="-121.716130"><ele>1276.7</ele><name>West Fork Salmon River, start of OSM Yellow Jacket Ski Trail</name><desc>source: OSM way 1289788302 west end; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 138; quote: turns south and goes downhill, paralleling the Snow Bunny Trail, then popping out onto the east clearcut road to cross the West Fork of the Salmon River</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.312980" lon="-121.696750"><ele>1446.4</ele><name>Salmon River crossing (high point)</name><desc>source: OSM way 1289788302 east end; DEM 4,804 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 139; book_elev_ft: 4800; quote: finally descends to the river, at 4,800 feet, which is crossed on snow</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.305430" lon="-121.687310"><ele>1416.2</ele><name>End of OSM Yellow Jacket Ski Trail</name><desc>source: OSM way 1289788303 south-east end; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 139; quote: Climb out of the canyon as the trail doubles back and descends through open forest.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.304820" lon="-121.685580"><ele>1395.1</ele><name>End of USFS SNO-663</name><desc>source: USFS SNO-663 (Yellowjacket Nordic) east end, DEM 4,577 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 139; quote: Climb out of the canyon as the trail doubles back and descends through open forest.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.306200" lon="-121.684200"><ele>1376.1</ele><name>Turn north at 4,500 ft</name><desc>source: placed on the DEM 4,500 ft contour in the draw north-east of the SNO-663 end; confidence: low; pdf_page: 139; book_elev_ft: 4500; quote: At the 4,500-foot level it turns left (north) and follows the contour toward the White River, reaching a meadow in about 600 yards.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.309500" lon="-121.681500"><ele>1368.6</ele><name>Meadow (600 yards on)</name><desc>source: placed 0.3 mi north along the 4,500 ft contour (DEM); no meadow mapped; confidence: low; pdf_page: 139; quote: At the 4,500-foot level it turns left (north) and follows the contour toward the White River, reaching a meadow in about 600 yards.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.310500" lon="-121.677500"><ele>1396.6</ele><name>Switchback right</name><desc>source: placed on the DEM, west rim of the gully above the sno-park; confidence: low; pdf_page: 139; quote: it finally switchbacks sharply to the right and descends a moderately steep slope into and out of a deep gully. Crossing gentle terrain, the trail passes near the Gravel Pit</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.306600" lon="-121.680100"><ele>1353.0</ele><name>Out of the gully, onto the track to the sno-park</name><desc>source: OSM track 394514520 (ski=yes) vertex; confidence: low; pdf_page: 139; quote: it finally switchbacks sharply to the right and descends a moderately steep slope into and out of a deep gully. Crossing gentle terrain, the trail passes near the Gravel Pit</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.303657" lon="-121.674434"><ele>1305.0</ele><name>White River West Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead th:white-river-west-sno-park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 139; quote: the trail passes near the Gravel Pit, which is on the other side of a low ridge, and soon ends at the White River West Sno-Park</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Yellowjacket Trail</name><desc>1. Mazama Sno-Park -&gt; Timberline road at Highway 26: straight (high), 0.07 mi | 2. Timberline road at Highway 26 -&gt; Trail leaves the Timberline road: osm (high), 0.16 mi | 3. Trail leaves the Timberline road -&gt; White Away Trail junction: osm (medium), 0.44 mi | 4. White Away Trail junction -&gt; Above the West Clearcut: straight (low), 0.55 mi | 5. Above the West Clearcut -&gt; Snow Bunny Trail crossing: straight (low), 0.32 mi | 6. Snow Bunny Trail crossing -&gt; West Fork Salmon River, start of OSM Yellow Jacket Ski Trail: usfs-trail (medium), 0.41 mi | 7. West Fork Salmon River, start of OSM Yellow Jacket Ski Trail -&gt; Salmon River crossing (high point): osm (high), 1.99 mi | 8. Salmon River crossing (high point) -&gt; End of OSM Yellow Jacket Ski Trail: osm (high), 0.76 mi | 9. End of OSM Yellow Jacket Ski Trail -&gt; End of USFS SNO-663: usfs-trail (medium), 0.17 mi | 10. End of USFS SNO-663 -&gt; Turn north at 4,500 ft: straight (low), 0.12 mi | 11. Turn north at 4,500 ft -&gt; Meadow (600 yards on): straight (low), 0.26 mi | 12. Meadow (600 yards on) -&gt; Switchback right: straight (low), 0.21 mi | 13. Switchback right -&gt; Out of the gully, onto the track to the sno-park: straight (low), 0.30 mi | 14. Out of the gully, onto the track to the sno-park -&gt; White River West Sno-Park: osm (medium), 0.44 mi</desc>
